Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip."ZipCode":     Zip‑level key for commuter counts  
• Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip."MetricID":     Identify the “60‑to‑89‑minutes” (B08303_011E) and “90‑or‑more‑minutes” (B08303_012E) commuter metrics  
• Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip."CensusValueByZip":  Numerical value of commuters for each MetricID‑Zip pair  
• LU_GeographyExpanded."ZipCode":          Bridge ZipCode to its state  
• LU_GeographyExpanded."PreferredStateAbbrev":  Filter for New York (“NY”) ZIP codes  
• Fact_StateBenchmark_ACS2021."MetricID":   Same commuter MetricIDs, but at the state level  
• Fact_StateBenchmark_ACS2021."StateBenchmarkValue":  New York’s total commuters for each MetricID  
• Fact_StateBenchmark_ACS2021."TotalStatePopulation": NY total population (appears on every NY row, pick any or MAX/MIN to return one value)  

Conditions that will be used  
• LU_GeographyExpanded."PreferredStateAbbrev" = 'NY'  
• MetricID IN ('B08303_011E', 'B08303_012E')  

----------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory‑to‑final Snowflake SQL queries
----------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Description:  See all metric tables whose IDs start with ‘B08303’ (Travel Time to Work).
SELECT DISTINCT 
       "MetricTableID",
       "MetricTableDesc"
FROM   CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusMetrics"
WHERE  "MetricTableID" = 'B08303'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description:  List the individual MetricIDs under table B08303 to locate “60–89” and “90+” minute commuters.
SELECT 
       "MetricID",
       "Descriptor1",
       "Descriptor2"
FROM   CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusMetrics"
WHERE  "MetricTableID" = 'B08303'
ORDER BY "MetricID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description:  Peek at ZIP‑level commuter counts for one of the long‑commute metrics (B08303_011E).
SELECT 
       "ZipCode",
       "MetricID",
       "CensusValueByZip"
FROM   CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip"
WHERE  "MetricID" = 'B08303_011E'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description:  Same peek but for the 90‑or‑more‑minutes metric.
SELECT 
       "ZipCode",
       "MetricID",
       "CensusValueByZip"
FROM   CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip"
WHERE  "MetricID" = 'B08303_012E'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description:  Distinct NY ZIP codes available in LU_GeographyExpanded (sanity check).
SELECT DISTINCT 
       "ZipCode"
FROM   CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."LU_GeographyExpanded"
WHERE  "PreferredStateAbbrev" = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description:  Combine commuter counts (60‑89 + 90+) for each NY ZIP; no ordering yet.
SELECT 
       z."ZipCode",
       SUM(z."CensusValueByZip") AS "Commute_60Plus"
FROM   CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip"  z
JOIN   CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."LU_GeographyExpanded"            g
       ON g."ZipCode" = z."ZipCode"
WHERE  g."PreferredStateAbbrev" = 'NY'
  AND  z."MetricID" IN ('B08303_011E','B08303_012E')
GROUP BY z."ZipCode"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description:  Same as #6 but ordered to see the largest totals first.
SELECT 
       z."ZipCode",
       SUM(z."CensusValueByZip") AS "Commute_60Plus"
FROM   CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip"  z
JOIN   CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."LU_GeographyExpanded"            g
       ON g."ZipCode" = z."ZipCode"
WHERE  g."PreferredStateAbbrev" = 'NY'
  AND  z."MetricID" IN ('B08303_011E','B08303_012E')
GROUP BY z."ZipCode"
ORDER BY "Commute_60Plus" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description:  Retrieve New York state‑level benchmark values for the same two MetricIDs.
SELECT 
       "MetricID",
       "StateBenchmarkValue",
       "TotalStatePopulation"
FROM   CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_StateBenchmark_ACS2021"
WHERE  "StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
  AND  "MetricID" IN ('B08303_011E','B08303_012E')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description:  Aggregate the two benchmark rows into a single “60‑plus‑minutes” state total.
SELECT 
       SUM("StateBenchmarkValue")  AS "NY_Benchmark_60Plus",
       MAX("TotalStatePopulation") AS "NY_TotalPopulation"
FROM   CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_StateBenchmark_ACS2021"
WHERE  "StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
  AND  "MetricID" IN ('B08303_011E','B08303_012E')
LIMIT 20;
